  {
    "title": "Kairos",
    "year": 2026,
	"released": "2016-10-08"
    "type": "LP",
    "band": "The Chilling Alpine Adventure",
    "tracks": [
      {
        "title": "Origins",
        "lyrics": "A fracture noticed in the corner\nWill it travel with the darkened storm?\nI dared to dream and waged the start of this for this to fall?\nTake all I’ve got, I can’t weather this all alone\nAnd what I’m not, you’ll make it whole\nStrike the flame in the face of the darkness\nDrift away to the way that her voice says\nI’ll stay awake, and I’ll wait for the origins\nA place for you and I to stay\nDon’t watch the clock for a moment,\nDon’t miss our love for an omen,\nHold me on through to the end\nFollow the wind when you’re fading\nIt will lead you through all of the ages\nHold me on through to the end\nTake all I’ve got, I can’t weather this all alone\nAnd what I’m not, you’ll make it whole\nIt’s all starting over\nI’m holding on to you\nNever let go"
      },
      {
        "title": "In Reverie",
        "lyrics": "The sun is setting\nI move around the lens to see red heaven\nA fold of arms around a wisp of smoke\nA place to rest but not the space I hoped\nMaybe I’m just lost in reverie,\nBut I’ll hold on to anything around me\nTwo lives, I need at least two lives\nTo run around this clock with you,\nGotta be at least two times\nI want to live twice with you\nShadow keeper, keep a steady eye on that pretty sleeper\nIn silver bays I’ll swim to meet her\nAnd in shivered waters clatter teeth\nTwo lives\nOh honey you ride out with the embers\nAnd I hear your whispers in the light curve\nYour spirit on fire just ahead of us\nPlease baby don’t lose me in the chaos"
      },
      {
        "title": "Kairos",
        "lyrics": "Hello, I was just born today\nNever before had I seen your face\nAd infinitum, ad silence\nI am only a traveler to wander through your wild,\nI am an astronomer, puzzled by your light\nKairos, we hold close to our days\nAnd follow the path down till we’re grey\nFrom blue light to small fires that we made\nKairos, we’ll hold on to these days\nHold on to me\nGood morning, the weather changed, we’ll stay in today\nDo you know that I had a dream where I was brave?\nI wish that were the case\nThere goes all my circuitry, nothing more to replace\nBut tomorrow I’ll be made again when I see your face\nI can’t breathe without you\nI can’t believe without you\nI can’t fight without you\nI can’t swim without you\nI can’t live without you"
      },
      {
        "title": "Blue Shift",
        "lyrics": "A Refrain\nIn ever dust, walk\nDown corridors,\nA wooden bird for you,\nSwept away into,\nMorning memory,\nThat time that you smiled at me,\nCan I return to it?\nGod, tell me it’s a place I can go back to,\nPlease"
      },
